@@ -120,7 +120,7 @@ wappi.pro API
 The app communicates with three external services via `UnityWebRequest` + coroutines (`IEnumerator` + `yield return SendWebRequest()`): Wappi (WhatsApp/Telegram transport, `Authorization` header), the self-hosted n8n (auth-free webhooks only), and RevenueCat via its SDK. The client carries NO server-side credentials except the wappi token (per-install proxy planned) — see the n8n section.
 
 ### A1 identity + transport (2026-09-17, audit remediation stage 1 — DEPLOYED to prod 2026-09-24, see the deploy note at the end of this section; runbook `docs/audits/a1-deploy-runbook.md`)
-The client holds NO Wappi credential any more. Every Wappi call is an allow-listed op sent to `/webhook/WappiProxy` and every n8n webhook carries `Authorization: Bearer <capability token>`; the server validates parameters, checks that every id belongs to the calling INSTALL, and forwards with its own `WappiAuthToken` credential. Pieces: `Assets/Scripts/Auth/` (`InstallSession` pure token model + refresh policy, `AuthClient` lazy always-active host: bootstrap/refresh single-flight, PlayerPrefs `CrAuth.*`, `AuthorizedRequest.Send(make, done)` = the ONE place the header is stamped + retry-once on 401, `ProfileClaim*` = legacy-profile claim), `Chat/WappiProxy` (`WappiProxy.Send(op, channel, args, done)` — Wappi's status+body pass through unchanged, so call sites keep their parsing). Server: `Tools/n8n/auth/{token,gate}.js` (HMAC-SHA256 `v1.` tokens, 12 h, claims `{i,u,p,w,c,e,n}`; verified in Code nodes WITHOUT a DB read because each Postgres node costs ≈1.9 s on prod), `build-auth-workflows.py` → `crAuthSession001` (bootstrap/refresh/claim.*) + `crWappiProxy0001`, `apply-auth-gate.py` (Auth Gate → Authorized? → 401/403 on all 12 client webhooks, `Bind Workflow Id`, `Register Upload`, owner-scoped Delete File, bot callback bound to the webhook path), `verify-auth-gate.py`, SQL `sql/2026-09-17-auth-installs.sql`. Server env: `NODE_FUNCTION_ALLOW_BUILTIN=crypto`, `N8N_BLOCK_ENV_ACCESS_IN_NODE=false`, `CR_AUTH_SECRET`, `CR_AUTH_COMPAT_UNTIL` (token-less LEGACY calls admitted only until that date). Rules: (1) a new client request site MUST go through `AuthorizedRequest.Send`/`WappiProxy.Send` — `AuthWiringGuardTests` fails on a direct `SendWebRequest` outside its allow-list or any `wappi.pro`/`Authorization` literal in transport code; (2) a new client webhook MUST be added to `GATED` in `apply-auth-gate.py` (with its ownership RULE) and to `PROTECTED_IDS`/the Validate list of Set Workflow State if it is infra; (3) a new Wappi operation MUST be added to the proxy's `OPS` allow-list (validated params, `profile_id ∈ p`), never a pass-through URL; (4) ownership = `bot_profiles.owner_id` (install) — RevenueCat `app_user_id` stays a billing key, never identity proof, and naming it grants nothing: it becomes the token's `u` only through `billing_bindings` (R2, 2026-09-27: one install per `$RCAnonymousID:` id — a device-id fallback is never bound; taken over only from a revoked holder or one without live bots; otherwise `u = null` + `billingConflict`, the gates refuse every billing-id field on `u = null`, Create WA/TG require a non-empty `AppUserID`, and the client never re-asks a declined id: `IdentityChanged` compares with `CrAuth.RequestedBillingId`); legacy/reinstalled profiles are claimed by PROOF, never assigned by a presented id — and since V2 (2026-09-28) the ONLY proof for ANY profile, owner-less ones included, is the code sent into the bot's own chat (`claim.start` → `claim.verify`). A pairing is a precondition that gives the claimant that chat, never a proof: Wappi does not say which link session completed a pairing, so the old time-window bind (`Bind Reauthed Profile`) handed an owner-less profile and its workflow to whoever had requested a QR when the OWNER reconnected independently — it is deleted, `claim.status` only ever answers `pending`/`reauth`/`owned`, and `Record Claim Pairing` (`claim_pair_by/at`) stays as an audit + stale-capability refusal. The code is guarded (`tests/test_claim.py` S11–S16, migration `sql/2026-10-07-claim-code-attempts.sql`): it counts as sent only when it was stored AND the transport accepted it (`Code Sent?` → else `Clear Claim Code` + `502 code_send_failed`, so a lost code is never «reused»); the pending install's fifth wrong answer kills it (`claim_code_locked`, 429, no new code until its 10-minute window ends); `claim.verify` never calls Wappi (`Needs Status?`); only `claim.start` takes a pending claim or starts its clock (status/verify polling never take one over); on Telegram the code goes to `account.phone` (the authorised account), never the top-level phone a claimant may have named in `auth/phone`. Client: after a pairing of a claim-pending profile `ProfileClaimFlow.AfterChannelAuthorized` raises the code sheet («Отменить», never «Позже») and the auth poller creates nothing unless it succeeded (`ProfileClaimWiringTests`); `NextUnowned` no longer skips pending claims. `claim.status` never sends a code and nothing of a claim is written before the install is verified (R1, 2026-09-27). (5) a refresh may answer 401 ONLY on Verify Install's positive verdict (`install_revoked`); any DB fault is 503 and `SessionRefreshPolicy.ShouldDiscardInstall` is the client's only wipe condition (R11). Isolated staging for all of this: `Tools/n8n/staging/` (private n8n home + Postgres from the `pgserver` wheel + Wappi MOCK on 127.0.0.1:8765; `bootstrap.py`, `e2e.py`, `e2e-auth.py`, run-scoped `fixtures.py`) — prod is read-only until the owner's explicit release go-ahead. **Deployed 2026-09-24 (owner's go, stages 0–7 in one pass; journal `docs/audits/implementation-progress.md`, snapshots `docs/audits/2026-09-24-prod-{before,after}.json`):** six SQL migrations through the `.secrets/sql-oneoff.py` harness, the seven env vars on the VPS (`CR_AUTH_COMPAT_UNTIL=2026-12-31T00:00:00Z`; the secret exists only in `~/choosereply/docker-compose.yml`), the 7 new workflows via `docker exec … n8n import:workflow` (ids preserved; sub-workflows `publish:workflow`, trigger workflows activated through the API), the 15 differing canonical workflows via `Tools/n8n/deploy-canonical.py` + `build-client-webhooks.py --update`, read-back all OK. Two facts to carry: prod runs Code nodes in TASK RUNNERS (`N8N_RUNNERS_ENABLED=true`, staging did not) — `require('crypto')` and `$env` were proven there with a self-deleting canary before anything was activated; and there are NO live bot clones on prod any more — «13» is archived (n8n refuses PUT on an archived workflow; `update-clones.py` now skips those